\h Haggai
\toc1 Haggai
\toc2 Haggai
\toc3 HAG
\mt2 This book contains the account of the Israeli people obeying God’s message to them through Haggai and rebuilding the temple. We call this book
\mt1 Haggai
\c 1
\s1 A call to rebuild the temple
\p
\v 1  \add I am\add*, Haggai, a prophet. I received a message from Yahweh on August 29th, during the second year that Darius was the king \add of Persia\add*. I told this message to Shealtiel’s son Zerubbabel, the governor of Judah, and to Jehozadak’s son Jeshua, the Supreme Priest.
\p
\v 2 Yahweh, the Commander of the armies of heaven, told \add me\add* that the people were saying that it was not yet time for them to rebuild Yahweh’s temple.
\p
\v 3 Then Yahweh gave me this message \add to tell to the people of Jerusalem\add*:
\v 4 “It is not right [RHQ] for you to be living in luxurious houses while my temple is only ruins!
\v 5  \add I,\add* Yahweh, the Commander of the armies of heaven, say this: Think about what is happening to you.
\v 6 You have planted a lot \add of seeds\add*, but you are not getting many \add crops\add* to harvest. You eat \add food\add*, but you never get enough. You drink \add wine\add*, but you are still thirsty. You wear clothes, but you do not stay warm. You earn money, \add but things are very expensive\add*, with the result that \add it is as though\add* [MET] \add your money disappears because\add* you are putting it in purses/pockets that have \add big\add* holes in them.”
\p
\v 7  \add So\add* this is what Yahweh, the Commander of the armies of heaven, says: “Think about what is happening to you.
\v 8  \add Then\add* go up into the hills, \add cut down trees,\add* and bring timber \add down here\add*, and rebuild my temple. When you do that, I will be pleased, and I will be honored.
\v 9 You expected \add to harvest\add* plenty \add of crops\add*, but there were few \add crops to harvest\add*. And when you brought the crops home, I caused them to spoil [IDM] quickly. The reason \add that happened is that\add* my temple is a ruins, while each of you are busy building your own \add beautiful\add* houses.
\v 10 It is because of what you \add are doing\add* that rain does not fall from the sky, and \add as a result\add* there are no crops.
\v 11 I have caused a ◄drought/severe lack of rain► on the hills and on your fields. The result has been that your grain \add has withered\add*, and your grapevines [MTY] and olive trees [MTY] and all your \add other\add* crops have dried up. \add Because of that,\add* you and your cattle \add do not have enough food\add*, and the hard work that you have done will be for nothing.”
\p
\v 12 Then Zerubbabel and Jeshua and all the others of God’s people who were still alive obeyed the message that Yahweh our God had said, and they heeded the message that I had given them, because \add they knew that\add* Yahweh our God had sent/appointed me. And the people revered Yahweh.
\p
\v 13 Then \add I\add*, Haggai, who was Yahweh’s messenger, gave this message from Yahweh to the people: “I, Yahweh, declare that I am with you.”
\v 14  \add So\add* Yahweh motivated Zerubbabel and Jeshua and the other people to want to rebuild the temple of our God, the Commander of the armies of angels. They gathered together and started to work to rebuild it.
\v 15  \add They started work\add* on September 21st, during the second year that Darius was the king.
\c 2
\s1 The new temple
\p
\v 1 On October 17 \add of that year\add*, Yahweh gave \add me\add*, the prophet Haggai, \add another\add* message.
\v 2  \add The message was that I should\add* say this to Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and to the other people who were still alive \add in Jerusalem\add*:
\v 3 “Do any of you remember how glorious our former temple was? \add If you do,\add* what does it look like to you now? It must seem like nothing at all.
\v 4 But now the Commander of the armies of angels says to \add all of you\add*, to Zerubbabel and Jeshua and the rest of you people who live in this nation, ‘\add Do not be discouraged;\add* be strong [DOU], and work \add to build this new temple\add*, because I will ◄be with/help► you.
\v 5 My Spirit remains among you, like I promised your \add ancestors\add* when they left Egypt. \add So\add* do not be afraid!’ ”
\p
\v 6 This is what the Commander of the armies of angels says: “Soon I will shake the sky and the earth, the oceans and the land again.
\v 7 I will shake \add again the people of \add* all the nations, and as a result they will bring their treasures \add to this temple\add*. I will fill this temple with \add my\add* glory.
\v 8 The silver and the gold \add that they own\add* are \add really\add* mine, \add so they will bring them to me\add*.
\v 9  \add Then\add* this temple will be more glorious than the former/previous \add temple was\add*. And I will cause things to go well for you all. \add That will surely happen because I,\add* the Commander of the armies of angels, have said it.”
\s1 What they do now will be acceptable to Yahweh
\p
\v 10 On December 18 of that year, Yahweh gave \add another\add* message to \add me\add*, the prophet Haggai.
\v 11 This is what the Commander of the armies of angels said to me: “Ask the priests \add this question\add* about what is written in the laws \add of Moses about sacrifices\add*:
\v 12 ‘If one \add of you priests takes from the altar some\add* meat that was sacrificed and is carrying it in his robes, if his robe touches \add some\add* bread or stew or wine or \add olive\add* oil or some other food, does that food also become ◄holy/acceptable for a sacrifice►?’”
\p \add When he said that to\add* the priests, they replied, “No.”
\p
\v 13 Then Haggai asked them, “If someone becomes unacceptable to God by touching a corpse, and \add then he\add* touches any of those foods, will the food \add also\add* become unacceptable to God?”
\p The priests replied, “Yes.”
\p
\v 14 Then Haggai replied, “Yahweh says \add this\add*: ‘It is the same with you people and with this nation. Everything that you do and \add all the sacrifices\add* that you all offer are unacceptable to me \add because of the sins that you have committed\add*.
\p
\v 15 Think about what has been happening to you before you began to lay the foundation of my temple.
\v 16 When you expected \add to harvest\add* 20 bushels \add of grain, you harvested\add* only ten bushels. When someone went to a \add big\add* wine vat to get 50 gallons \add of wine\add*, there were only 20 \add gallons in the vat\add*.
\v 17 I sent ◄blight/hot winds► and mildew and hail to destroy all your crops. But still you did not return to me.
\p
\v 18 Starting from this day, December 18, the day when \add you\add* have laid the foundation of my \add new\add* temple, continue to think carefully \add about your situation\add*.
\v 19 Is there now [RHQ] \add any grain\add* seed left in your barns? \add No, because you have eaten the small amount that you harvested\add*. And there is no fruit on your grapevines and fig trees and pomegranate \add trees\add* and olive trees.
\p But, from now on, I will bless you!’ ”
\s1 Yahweh’s promise to Zerubbabel
\p
\v 20 On that same day, Yahweh gave another message to me.
\v 21  \add He said,\add* “Tell Zerubbabel the governor of Judah that I am going to shake the sky and the earth.
\v 22 I will end the power of the kings of \add many\add* nations [DOU]. I will cause their chariots and their drivers, their horses and \add the soldiers\add* who are riding on them to be destroyed. \add What will happen is that I will cause the soldiers\add* to kill each other with their swords.
\p
\v 23 Zerubbabel, you serve \add me well\add*. So \add I\add*, the Commander of the armies of angels, declare that \add like kings wear\add* signet rings \add to show that they have authority to rule people\add*, I will appoint you and cause you \add to have authority to rule\add*. I will do that because I have chosen you. \add That will surely happen because I,\add* the Commander of the armies of angels, have said it.”
